   "text": "# Network Diagnostic Tool\n\nA beginner-friendly Python tool that performs basic network checks (ping, DNS lookup) on a list of hosts and saves results to CSV.\n\n## ✨ Features\n- Ping test for each host (latency in ms)\n- DNS resolution (host → IP address)\n- Marks unreachable/unresolved hosts\n- Saves results with timestamp to `network_report.csv`\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start\n1. Clone repo and install Python 3.9+\n2. Add hosts to `hosts.txt`\n3. Run:\n   ```bash\n   python main.py\n   ```\n4. Open `network_report.csv`\n\n## 🧪 Example Output\n| Host        | IP Address   | Latency (ms) | Timestamp           |\n|-------------|--------------|--------------|---------------------|\n| google.com  | 142.250.72.46| 22           | 2025-08-16 14:01:12 |\n| github.com  | 140.82.113.3 | 31           | 2025-08-16 14:01:13 |\n| 8.8.8.8     | 8.8.8.8      | 18           | 2025-08-16 14:01:14 |\n\n## 📄 License\nMIT\n",
